; Contiguous-access detection for outer-loop vectorization when the access
; address depends on the inner-loop induction variable. The address SCEV is a
; nested AddRec {{base,+,outer-step}<outer>,+,inner-step<inner>}; the access is
; consecutive w.r.t. the vectorized outer loop iff its outer-loop step is one
; element. Recognizing this requires lowering the (widened) inner-loop header
; phi to an AddRec, which getSCEVExprForVPValue does via the HeaderVPBBToLoop
; map threaded in by tryToConvertVPInstructionsToVPRecipes.
;
; Safety check disabled: the symbolic trip count M needs a runtime M >= VF guard
; (added later) to prove these collision-free.

; --- column-major store: A[i + j*M] ---
; for (i = 0; i < N; i++)
;   for (j = 0; j < M; j++)
;     A[i + j*M] *= 2;
